# #5841: an epoch-only append is fenced only by the WAL shard's entry check against
# the donor's epoch.
MODULE: HandOffBoundEpochOnlyWriteUnfenced
TARGET: HandOffBound
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the WAL shard allocates an epoch-only append whatever its epoch, so a superseded duplicate's write is never refused
PERTURBS: DupAlloc, DupReject
BOUNDS: WithStaleDonor = TRUE, WithPreArm = TRUE, MaxWindows = 1

--- FIND
    /\ dpend
    /\ dstamp >= eRow
    /\ next < MaxOff
--- REPLACE
    /\ dpend
\* MUTATION: no entry check for an epoch-only append.
    /\ next < MaxOff
--- END

--- FIND
    /\ dpend
    /\ dstamp < eRow
    /\ dpend' = FALSE
--- REPLACE
    /\ dpend
\* MUTATION: never refused.
    /\ FALSE
    /\ dpend' = FALSE
--- END
